  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Prime-factor devissage",
  "statement": "Let $n>1$, choose a prime $r\\mid n$, and let $F$ be killed by $n$. There is a\nnatural exact sequence\n\n$$\n 0\\longrightarrow F[r]\\longrightarrow F\n \\xrightarrow{r} rF\\longrightarrow0,\n$$\n\nwhere $F[r]$ is killed by $r$ and $rF$ is killed by $n/r$. Thus a property of\ntorsion sheaves [def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves] stable under short exact\nsequences and known for prime-torsion sheaves holds for every sheaf killed by\na positive integer.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-iff/lem-weil-pbc-prime-factor-devissage.md",
    "place": "node lem-weil-pbc-prime-factor-devissage, order 1086"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "The displayed sequence is the kernel--image sequence for multiplication by\n$r$ in the abelian category of etale sheaves, whose kernels and images are\ncomputed sectionwise as in [def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves]. The claims about the\norders follow from $r\\cdot F[r]=0$ and $n/r\\cdot rF=0$. The induction on the\nnumber $\\sum_\\ell v_\\ell(n)$ of prime factors of $n$, using this sequence at\neach step, proves the stability assertion.",
      "uses": [
        "def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
  "proof_deps": [
    "def-weil-pbc-etale-sheaves"
  ],
